<title>USA: PacifiCorp, Destec complete acquisition.</title>
<headline>PacifiCorp, Destec complete acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>PacifiCorp said a consortium of energy producers including it, National Power Plc, Destec Energy Inc and the Commonwealth Bank Group of Australia have completed the acquisition of a Victoria, Australia, power station for about $1.9 billion.</p>
<p>It said the consortium, known as Hazelwood Power, financed the purchase of the 1,600 megawatt generating station and associated coal mine with about $858 million in equity contributions and $1 billion of non-recourse borrowings.</p>
<p>PacifiCorp's portion of the equity investment was about $155 million.  </p>
<p>National Power will oversee Hazelwood plant operations and PacifiCorp will oversee operations at the adjacent Hazelwood mine, it said.</p>
